Note: a week of temperatures: average, spread, warmest day and a small chart.

set days to "Mon", "Tue", "Wed", "Thu", "Fri", "Sat" and "Sun".
set temps to 21.5, 23.0, 19.8, 25.4, 24.1, 18.9 and 22.7.

set mean to the average of temps.
set total to 0.0.
for every t in temps, add (t minus mean) squared to total.
set spread to the square root of (total divided by the number of items in temps).

say "Average:" and then mean with 2 decimals and then "°C".
say "Spread:" and then spread with 2 decimals and then "°C".
say "From" and then the smallest of temps and then "to" and then the largest of temps and then "°C".

set warm to every t in temps where t is more than mean.
say "Days above average:" and then the number of items in warm.

say "".
for every i from 1 to the number of items in days
  set t to item i of temps.
  set bar to "#" repeated (t minus 15) rounded times.
  say item i of days padded to 4 and then t with 1 decimals padded on the left to 5 and then " " and then bar.
that's all.
